SUMMARY:What’s happenin’
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**For Nov 19 thru Nov 25**\n.\nUpcoming **m
 usic events** may be found here:\nhttps://www.facebook.com/hendolivemusic/
 \n(Updates on Thurs morning)\n.\n**Assorted entertainment\, festival & mar
 ket events may be found here:**\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/calenda
 r-of-events\n.\n**Library programs** may be found here:\nhttps://henderson
 pl.libcal.com/\nTech classes\, adult programs\, interesting stuff.. 😉\n
 .\n**Every Thursday\; Nov 19**\nCountry Line Dance Lesson\n7-9pm\, Honeysu
 ckle Holler\, 101 East Allen St\, Hendersonville NC 28792\nCost: $5 per pe
 rson.\n.\n**Every Friday\; Nov 20**\nCountry Dance Lesson - Style Varies\n
 7-8pm\, Honeysuckle Holler\, 101 East Allen St\, Hendersonville NC 28792\n
 Cost: $5 per person.\n.\n**Hospice Warehouse sale\; Nov 20 & 21. (**(3rd F
 ri/Sat of mnth)\nYou'll find a wide variety of value furniture items at th
 e warehouse. Shop with us each month when we host our 2-day warehouse sale
 s and support the care services of Four Seasons.\n9:00 AM - 2:00 PM\; 561 
 S Allen Rd\, Flat Rock\nhttps://www.facebook.com/HospiceHomeStore\n.\n**No
 vember 20** @ 10:00 am - 2:00 pm\; Free\nHandmade Holidays Craft Fair & Ma
 rket\nPurchase holiday gifts from Carolina Village residents and staff\,\n
 in our Fireplace Lounge & Village Hall\nFree parking and free entry!\nCraf
 ters & artists will be offering handmade:\n• Fine art\; Paper crafts\; T
 eddy bears\; Artisan Santas\; Fiber arts\; Jewelry\; Wreaths\; Stationery\
 ; Décor\; Books\;\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/handmade-holid
 ays-craft-fair-market\n.\n**Saturday\, November 21**\nThe Showboat Band (N
 o Cover)\n3:30-6:30pm\, Point Lookout Vineyards\, 408 Appleola Road\, Hend
 ersonville\n.\n**Saturday\, November 21**\nJohnny Blackwell & the Jukebox 
 Brothers\n7-9pm\, Guidon Brewery\, 415 8th Ave. East\, Hendersonville\n.\n
 **November 21** @ 9:00 am - 1:00 pm\nThanksgiving Holiday Market at the He
 ndersonville Farmers Market\n9am-1pm at the historic Train Depot. It’s y
 our chance to discover one-of-a-kind gifts\, holiday decorations\, and del
 ectable treats for your feasts. With over 30 enthusiastic vendors\, this i
 s a can’t-miss event.\n.\n**November 21\; 10:00 am - 5:00 pm\; Free**\nJ
 eter Mountain Farm Christmas\nkeepsake hot chocolate to a holiday hard cid
 er\, live Christmas jazz music to rocking chairs around the fire\,\nXmas T
 rees available by reservation…\nhttps://www.jetermountainfarm.com/attrac
 tions/christmas\n.\n**Saturday\, November 21**\nMountain Shag Club Thanksg
 iving Party (With DJ “Big Fish” Calhoun)\n6-10pm\, Hendersonville Elks
  Lodge\, 546 North Justice St\, Hendersonville NC 28739\nManna Food Bank F
 undraiser – Please bring $$ or non-perishable food items to donate.\nBri
 ng a snack to share and 50/50 raffle. FREE for members and $10 for Guests.
 \n.\n**Sunday\, Nov 22**\nHendersonville Ballroom Dance Club Tea Dance - A
 ttire: Casual Dress\n3-5:30pm\, Upstairs at Hedrick Rhodes Veterans Center
 \, 900 North Main St\, Hendersonville NC 28792\nOur dances are open to the
  public and everyone is invited. Enjoy Ballroom Dancing to the music of DJ
  Gary Bills who plays a variety of dance tunes including Swing (East & Wes
 t Coast)\, Waltz\, Tango\, Rumba\, Cha-Cha and Foxtrot. There is also a da
 nce mixer Cost: $5 per person at door.\n.\n**Thu\; November 26** @ 8:30 am
  - 10:30 am\nHendersonville’s 14th Annual Turkey Trot 5k\n$28.00 – $38
 .00\nKick off your Thanksgiving with a fun-filled dash through Hendersonvi
 lle at the 14th annual Turkey Trot to **benefit Hope Coalition!** Whether 
 you are a seasoned runner\, casual stroller\, or just in it for the costum
 es\, this event is open to all-ages!\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/ev
 ent/hendersonvilles-14th-annual-turkey-trot-5k\n.\n**November 27** @ 7:30 
 pm - 10:00 pm\; $$$\nA Flat Rock Playhouse Christmas Show – 10th Anniver
 sary Special\nCelebrate ten dazzling years of holiday cheer at Flat Rock P
 layhouse!\nFor a decade\, A Flat Rock Playhouse Christmas has been the che
 rished gathering that brings our community together\, where Broadway spark
 le meets small-town heart and the spirit of the season takes center stage.
 \nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/a-flat-rock-playhouse-christmas-
 show-10th-anniversary-special/2026-11-27\nhttps://www.flatrockplayhouse.or
 g/\n.\n**November 28**\nSmall Business Saturday\nPlan your Christmas shopp
 ing downtown. A gift from a local business is a gift made or sold with lov
 e. Support our downtown businesses on Small Business Saturday and all holi
 day season\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/small-business-Saturda
 y\nhttps://www.hendersonvillenc.gov/events/holiday-cheer-downtown-henderso
 nville\n.\n**November 28** @ 8:00 am - 2:00 pm\; Free\nHenderson County Cu
 rb Market Christmas Open House\nThe Henderson County Curb Market celebrate
 s the holiday with a Christmas Open House. Visitors will enjoy a drop-in a
 ppearance from Santa and his elf\, complimentary cookies\, hot cider and h
 ot chocolate\, a raffle basket\, a children’s activity table\, a local a
 uthors signing\, a Native American story teller and the community Peppermi
 nt Bear scavenger hunt. There is shopping for the perfect hand crafted gif
 ts created by local vendors\, greenery\, holiday decorations\, seasonal pr
 oduce\, fresh baked goods\, honey\, preserve and relishes.\nhttps://visith
 endersonvillenc.org/event/henderson-county-curb-market-christmas-open-hous
 e\n.\n**Sunday\, November 29**\nSundayFunday with Peggy Ratusz & Friends\n
 4-6pm\, Southern Appalachian Brewery\, 822 Locust St\, Hendersonville\n.\n
 These are NOT hosted events and are posted for informational purposes only
 . Please make personal arrangements to meetup with friends and family.\nIf
  you wish to attend and host one of these events\, I will post the event a
 s an individual happening. Hosting only requires being focal point for oth
 ers and making introductions. Simple!!
